  "notes": [
    "Cert canonical signed payload = be64(uid) || be64(expires_at_ms) || ASCII bytes of the sender_pub BASE64 STRING (not the decoded key). Signed by the server Ed25519 key (GET /api/sealed-sender/server-key → {publicKey}). The server key here is a TEST stand-in; production certs come from POST /api/sealed-sender/cert {senderPub}. Go Cert JSON tags: uid, expires_at_ms, sender_pub, sig. Validity = 24h (sealedsender.go:54).",
    "verifyCert rejects when Date.now() > expires_at_ms (equal is still valid).",
    "blob = b64( nonce(24) || ephemeralPub(32) || nacl.box(UTF-8 JSON.stringify({cert, ratchet}), nonce, recipientIdentityPub, ephemeralPriv) ). NOTE the ORDER: nonce FIRST, then ephemeral pub — the OPPOSITE of the server OSB1 format (offlineSeal.json).",
    "sealEnvelope draws the ephemeral keypair (32) BEFORE the nonce (24).",
    "`ratchet` is the ratchet envelope JSON STRING (despite the parameter name ratchetCiphertextB64). WS frame: {\"type\":\"p2p-sealed\",\"data\":{\"toUserId\",\"messageId\",\"blob\",\"deliveryToken\"}}; deliveryToken is an opaque server HMAC token (GET /api/sealed-sender/delivery-token/<recipientId>) and mandatory since build 179.",
    "Receiver MUST verifyCert (with one forced server-key refresh on failure, sealedSender.ts:252) and then ratchet-decrypt inner.ratchet with the ratchet state keyed by cert.uid."
  ],
